    {
      "type": "tweet",
      "id": "2093446043035992118",
      "url": "https://x.com/agarwl_/status/2093446043035992118",
      "twitterUrl": "https://twitter.com/agarwl_/status/2093446043035992118",
      "text": "I don't know if the mopd idea works but feels like it has to work.  \n\nIt's somewhat intuitive: if you distill a model directly, you are distilling all it's shortcomings too (especially true if it's a RL'ed teacher model distilled to a much bigger student LLM)\n\nBut if you distill the improvement direction post RL, you don't have to get the shortcomings. This does assume that the improvement direction is approx similar across same family of models.",
      "source": "Twitter for Android",
      "retweetCount": 0,
      "replyCount": 0,
      "likeCount": 5,
      "quoteCount": 0,
      "viewCount": 547,
      "createdAt": "Fri Aug 28 21:10:05 +0000 2026",
      "lang": "en",
      "bookmarkCount": 2,
      "isReply": true,
      "inReplyToId": "2093443390474211391",
      "conversationId": "2093430306804044033",
